ture, lighting, textiles, d\u00e9cor, umbrellas, and fire pits. It also provides bath product assortment comprising vanities and storage pieces, faucets and hardware, and Turkish bath towels; lighting fixtures, including chandeliers, pendants, table and floor lamps, and sconces; indoor and outdoor rugs, bed linens, and pillows and throws; and d\u00e9cor products, such as wall art, mirrors, vases, candles, and other decorative accessories. The company distributes its products through an omni-channel model comprising showrooms, ecommerce, catalogs and digital media, interior designer services, trade services, and client engagement. Arhaus, Inc. was founded in 1986 and is headquartered in Boston Heights, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John P. Reed | Founder, Chairman, President & CEO | Age 70 | Compensation: $4.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $511K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 15%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $22K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Arhaus, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $2.0B market cap on $1.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 92% against a 12% cost of capital \u2014 a 80-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 41%.","The business throws off $59M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.03\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 18\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.7% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 3 other valuation measures)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9386973180076628},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $3.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 30% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Among the least levered in Consumer Cyclical \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Arhaus forecasts FY2026 net revenue of $1.465B-$1.485B while targeting 25% e-commerce penetration over 5 years (NASDAQ:ARHS)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4667755-arhaus-forecasts-fy2026-net-revenue-of-1_465b-1_485b-while-targeting-25-percent-e-commerce","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793939858.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.25,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Arhaus Inc (ARHS) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Highlights: Record Revenue and Surging Written Sales ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/arhaus-inc-arhs-q3-2026-231520808.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793920520.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.077,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Arhaus (ARHS) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/arhaus-arhs-q3-2026-earnings-204540000.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793912202.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.128,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"What Arhaus (ARHS) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/arhaus-arhs-said-q3-earnings-181505224.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793902505.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.542,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Here's What Key Metrics Tell Us About Arhaus, Inc. (ARHS) Q3 Earnings","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024158/here-s-what-key-metrics-tell-us-about-arhaus-inc-arhs-q3-earnings?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm-30241